  "body": "Since PR #160 (#140: sideways rapids marched along their whole length), crates/sim/tests/overhang_laws.rs fails 3 tests on main: `a_2d_path_without_a_model_is_unchanged`, `the_same_rapid_above_the_ledge_is_clean` and `the_same_rapid_beside_a_post_without_a_ledge_is_clean`. PR #160's gate ran vertical_rapids, radial_rapids and sideways_rapids, but not overhang_laws.\n\nReading: `rapid_under(z)` cuts two floor slots along X 17 (Y 45→8.5 and Y -25→-8.5), then rapids from Y -8.5 to 45 at z. Y ∈ [-8.5, 8.5] at X 17 is never cut. The fixture's comment says the rapid's 'three column samples are all cleared' - the start/mid/end gap #140 fixed. So the march most likely finds real uncut stock, and these fixtures were written around the old gap.\n\nDone means: confirm with evidence whether each conviction is real (fixture wrong) or false (march wrong), then fix accordingly. If the fixtures are wrong, they get a cleared column under the whole rapid that still leaves the hidden band under the ledge, so the overhang law's own tests (the rapid under the ledge convicted, above it clean, beside a bare post clean) keep testing the overhang law and not the column law.",
